>> title: Bagels
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, bagels, boiled, malt, breakfast
>> counters: Deli, Bakery
>> servings: 8
>> time: 15 hr
>> step.1: stir until the malt dissolves
>> step.2: add flour and salt, knead 10 min, rise 1 hour
>> step.3: divide into eight rings, chill overnight
>> step.4: boil 1 min a side
>> step.5: top, bake 475°F 20 min

Stir @warm water{1 1/4%cup}(295 g) with @barley malt syrup{2%Tbs}(40 g) and @instant yeast{2%tsp}(6 g).

Add @bread flour{4%cup}(540 g) and @table salt{2%tsp}(12 g) to @&(~1)mixture{}, then knead ~{10%min} to a stiff dough and rise ~{1%hour}.

Divide @&(~1)dough{} into eight rings and refrigerate ~{12%hours}.

Boil @&(~1)bagels{} for ~{1%min} a side in water with @baking soda{1%Tbs}(14 g) and @barley malt syrup{2%Tbs}(40 g).

Top @&(~1)bagels{} with @everything seasoning{3%Tbs}(or sesame or poppy seeds) and bake at 475°F for ~{20%min}.
